// `#in A B C` -- a block that runs in ANY of the listed states (OR-gate, built
// from an OP_NINSTATE chain + a terminating OP_INSTATE). `hit` counts the cycles
// the shared block runs: it advances a -> b, then b -> c, so the block fires in
// a and in b (hit reaches 2) and then stops once State is c. Runs seq + reactive
// to prove the NINSTATE OR-chain (sequential) and the folded State==a||State==b
// per-rule condition (reactive) agree.
#states a b c
#variable hit = 0

#in INIT
  State = a
#end
#in a b
  hit = hit + 1
  State = b ? State == a
  State = c ? State == b
#end
